---
// Veterans contact sheet (#228, part of #210): the VA clinic and Vet Center on
// Commerce Drive, what needs a trip to Clarksburg, and 24/7 lines. Claims help,
// jobs, posts and burial added in #586, #588, #589, #590 and #591 (research:
// docs/groups/veterans.md). Facts read 2026-10-30.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ResourceCard from '../components/ResourceCard.astro';
import { loadDir } from '../lib/content.mjs';
import { FIX_FORM } from '../lib/group-requests.mjs';
export const page = { door: "family", topic: "veterans", label: "Veterans", summary: "The VA clinic and Vet Center, free help with a VA claim, jobs, posts, burial benefits, and 24/7 help lines" };
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const all = loadDir('resources');
const r = (slug) => all.find((e) => e.slug === slug);
---
<Base title="Veterans in Morgantown and Mon County: VA clinic, Vet Center and help lines" description="The Monongalia County VA Clinic and the Morgantown Vet Center on Commerce Drive, free help filing a VA claim, veteran job help, Legion and VFW posts in Morgantown, burial benefits and veterans cemeteries, and 24/7 lines for crisis and housing help.">
  <h1>Help for veterans in Mon County</h1>
  <p class="lede">Two VA offices are on Commerce Drive, off US 19: a health clinic and a Vet Center for counseling. In a crisis, dial 988 and press 1, any time.</p>

  {r('veterans-crisis-line') && <h2>In a crisis</h2>}
  {r('veterans-crisis-line') && <ResourceCard r={r('veterans-crisis-line')} sms="838255" smsLabel="Veterans Crisis Line" />}

  <h2>Health care: the VA clinic</h2>
  <p>For care this clinic does not offer, VA Clarksburg's main medical center is in Clarksburg (address and phone below). The VA works with Disabled American Veterans and county veterans affairs directors on van rides to scheduled medical appointments. Ask the clinic about rides (<a href="https://www.va.gov/clarksburg-health-care/locations/monongalia-county-va-clinic/">source</a>).</p>
  {r('monongalia-county-va-clinic') && <ResourceCard r={r('monongalia-county-va-clinic')} showCost />}

  <h2>Counseling: the Vet Center</h2>
  <p>Free and confidential, and not a medical office.</p>
  {r('morgantown-vet-center') && <ResourceCard r={r('morgantown-vet-center')} />}

  <h2>Filing a VA claim: free help</h2>
  <p>You do not have to pay anyone to file a VA claim. VA says help from an accredited representative of a Veterans Service Organization is always free. Accredited attorneys and claims agents can charge a fee only after VA decides your first claim, and only with a fee agreement you signed. Before you get help, make sure the person is accredited with VA (<a href="https://www.va.gov/resources/va-accredited-representative-faqs/">VA</a>).</p>
  {r('wvdva-clarksburg-benefit-office') && <ResourceCard r={r('wvdva-clarksburg-benefit-office')} />}
  {r('huntington-va-regional-benefit-office') && <ResourceCard r={r('huntington-va-regional-benefit-office')} />}
  <p>To find any accredited representative near you, use VA's <a href="https://www.va.gov/get-help-from-accredited-representative/find-rep/">find a representative</a> tool.</p>

  <h2>Finding a job</h2>
  <p>WorkForce West Virginia gives veterans priority of service: veterans and eligible spouses who qualify get early access to job listings, plus help with resumes, interviews and training. When you register, fill out the military history section (<a href="https://workforcewv.org/job-seeker/specialized-services/veterans/">WorkForce WV</a>).</p>
  {r('workforce-wv-morgantown-office') && <ResourceCard r={r('workforce-wv-morgantown-office')} />}
  {r('owh-veteran-job-help') && <ResourceCard r={r('owh-veteran-job-help')} />}
  <p>The Morgantown Vet Center can also help with Veteran Readiness and Employment (VR&amp;E), the VA program for job training and work help (<a href="https://www.va.gov/morgantown-vet-center/">VA</a>).</p>

  <h2>Meet other veterans</h2>
  <p>Posts in Morgantown, from each group's own post finder. Times can change, so call or check the finder first.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>American Legion Mountaineer Post 174</strong>, 3472 Earl Core Road. <a href="tel:13042914676">304-291-4676</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>American Legion Monongalia Post 2</strong>, Old Cheat Road. No phone listed.</li>
    <li><strong>VFW Post 548, Gen. Daniel Morgan Post</strong>. Meets at 494 Spruce Street, 8 p.m. on the 1st and 3rd Thursday. <a href="tel:13042923927">304-292-3927</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>VFW Post 9916, John L. Frazier Post</strong>, 340 Holland Avenue. Meets 7 p.m. on the 1st Thursday. <a href="tel:13042965981">304-296-5981</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="meta">Sources: the <a href="https://www.wvlegion.org/locator/">American Legion Department of West Virginia post locator</a> and the <a href="https://www.vfw.org/find-a-post">VFW post finder</a>, checked October 30, 2026. The state's <a href="https://veterans.wv.gov/basic-block/veteran-service-organizations">list of veterans groups</a> has more.</p>

  <h2>Losing your housing, or already homeless</h2>
  {r('va-homeless-veterans-line') && <ResourceCard r={r('va-homeless-veterans-line')} />}

  <h2>When a veteran dies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Burial costs:</strong> VA pays up to $2,000 toward burial for a death connected to service (after September 11, 2001). For a death not connected to service on or after October 1, 2026, VA pays up to $1,032 toward burial and up to $1,032 for a plot. Amounts are lower for earlier deaths. See the full rules and how to apply at <a href="https://www.va.gov/burials-memorials/veterans-burial-allowance/">VA</a>. The state's burial page lists older amounts, so go by VA's page.</li>
    <li><strong>Headstone or marker:</strong> VA gives a government headstone or marker for an eligible veteran's grave at no charge (<a href="https://veterans.wv.gov/benefits-assistance/benefits/burial-benefits">WVDVA</a>).</li>
    <li><strong>Help paying to set the marker:</strong> the state's Jack Bennett Fund gives up to $380 toward installing it, based on the family's need. Family members, funeral directors and cemeteries can apply (<a href="https://veterans.wv.gov/benefits-assistance/benefits/burial-benefits">WVDVA</a>).</li>
  </ul>
  {r('wv-national-cemetery') && <ResourceCard r={r('wv-national-cemetery')} />}
  {r('kinnard-state-veterans-cemetery') && <ResourceCard r={r('kinnard-state-veterans-cemetery')} showCost />}

  <p>Other help near home, for anyone: <a href="tel:211">call 211</a> for food, bills and housing help, or see <a href={`${base}/turning-65/`}>Turning 65 or on Medicare</a>.</p>

  <p class="meta">VA sources checked October 30, 2026. Call before you go, since hours can change. We describe these services; we do not handle VA claims or speak for the VA or any veterans group. Something out of date? <a href={FIX_FORM}>Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
